From a1318465b65a1280ee27d73749fba72c33e75d18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Macktherealonereally <macdev@mackthessd.org>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:03:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] o1s: display: Use AOSP default fast brightness ramp rates

The display config set the "fast" ramp rates to 0.06 per second (in
HLG-space units). That is slower than the "slow" auto-brightness
adaptation of most devices and about 12x slower than the AOSP default.
AOSP uses config_brightness_ramp_rate_fast = 180, which
BrightnessSynchronizer.brightnessIntToFloat maps to
(180-1)/(255-1) = 0.7047244. The fast rate is used for
non-auto-brightness transitions: waking from AoD or dim, user activity
after the dim timeout, and policy changes. So each of those crawled up
to the 3 s screenBrightnessRampIncreaseMaxMillis cap.

Restore the AOSP default for the fast rates. The slow rates (0.04/s),
which pace ambient-light adaptation, and the 3 s caps stay as they
are.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 configs/display/displayconfig.xml | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configs/display/displayconfig.xml b/configs/display/displayconfig.xml
index 07b4f4c..f9a83f0 100644
--- a/configs/display/displayconfig.xml
+++ b/configs/display/displayconfig.xml
@@ -34,8 +34,8 @@
             </point>
         </sdrHdrRatioMap>
     </highBrightnessMode>
-    <screenBrightnessRampFastDecrease>0.06</screenBrightnessRampFastDecrease>
-    <screenBrightnessRampFastIncrease>0.06</screenBrightnessRampFastIncrease>
+    <screenBrightnessRampFastDecrease>0.7047244</screenBrightnessRampFastDecrease>
+    <screenBrightnessRampFastIncrease>0.7047244</screenBrightnessRampFastIncrease>
     <screenBrightnessRampSlowDecrease>0.04</screenBrightnessRampSlowDecrease>
     <screenBrightnessRampSlowIncrease>0.04</screenBrightnessRampSlowIncrease>
     <screenBrightnessRampIncreaseMaxMillis>3000</screenBrightnessRampIncreaseMaxMillis>
-- 
